The attached image is Figure 11 from the PDF, illustrating the histological appearance of injection sites two weeks after intramuscular administration of aluminum hydroxide adjuvant (AH) or Nano-11. The image on the left, labeled AH, shows extensive granulomatous inflammation (asterisks) within the skeletal muscle (M), indicative of a persistent inflammatory response. In contrast, the image on the right, labeled Nano-11, reveals significantly less residual inflammation (asterisk) within the muscle (M), demonstrating that Nano-11 induces a more transient and localized inflammatory reaction compared to aluminum hydroxide. This highlights Nano-11's potential for a better safety profile.